From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Meiser <peter.meiser@gmx.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:04:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sshd: Tolerate a NULL privsep pw_passwd

bionic's getpwnam() returns Android IDs such as SSH_PRIVSEP_USER
("shell") with pw_passwd NULL, and pwcopy() keeps it NULL. sshd then
crashed in strlen() while wiping it, right after "sshd version",
whenever it ran as root. Only wipe a password that is there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I8d5b9c897773c469909ca25aff3b233f6039d733
---
 sshd.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sshd.c b/sshd.c
index fba25e6..ce00dda 100644
--- a/sshd.c
+++ b/sshd.c
@@ -1760,7 +1760,10 @@ main(int ac, char **av)
 			    SSH_PRIVSEP_USER);
 	} else {
 		privsep_pw = pwcopy(privsep_pw);
-		freezero(privsep_pw->pw_passwd, strlen(privsep_pw->pw_passwd));
+		/* bionic's getpwnam() leaves pw_passwd NULL. */
+		if (privsep_pw->pw_passwd != NULL)
+			freezero(privsep_pw->pw_passwd,
+			    strlen(privsep_pw->pw_passwd));
 		privsep_pw->pw_passwd = xstrdup("*");
 	}
 #if !defined(ANDROID)
-- 
2.53.0

